invariant: INV-49
file: keccak_avx2.c
catches: test/lint-frame-align.sh
reason: keccak_avx2_permute loses the attribute that makes clang align its
  frame to 32 bytes. The state is 25 vectors and AVX2 has 16 registers, so
  the rounds store and reload lanes in 32-byte stack slots, and clang then
  places those slots 16 bytes past a multiple of 32 for half of all
  callers' stacks: a call took 675 ns there on an EPYC 7763 where an
  aligned frame took 441, and up to 1,228 ns with a slot across a page
  boundary. The streams are the same bytes, so bin/mlkem_avx2_equiv_test
  passes, and CI compiles with gcc, which aligns the frame on its own.

--- old
__attribute__((force_align_arg_pointer)) void keccak_avx2_permute(keccak_x4 *s) {
--- new
void keccak_avx2_permute(keccak_x4 *s) {
